  "segments": [
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0001",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 0.57,
      "end_seconds": 4.03,
      "duration_seconds": 3.46,
      "text": "Sorry I'm a little late, doctor."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0002",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 4.95,
      "end_seconds": 10.22,
      "duration_seconds": 5.27,
      "text": "You're alright, take a seat. What can I do for you?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0003",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 11.21,
      "end_seconds": 20.07,
      "duration_seconds": 8.86,
      "text": "Oh, mainly a new headache at the temple. There's a couple of other things, but that's the main one."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0004",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 20.7,
      "end_seconds": 23.96,
      "duration_seconds": 3.26,
      "text": "Shall I check your blood pressure and pulse?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0005",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 36.34,
      "end_seconds": 39.07,
      "duration_seconds": 2.73,
      "text": "So, sit still for a moment..."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0006",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 48.62,
      "end_seconds": 55.36,
      "duration_seconds": 6.74,
      "text": "Okay: saturation 99 percent, pressure 125 over 69, pulse 66. And respiratory rate 17."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0007",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 57.17,
      "end_seconds": 58.84,
      "duration_seconds": 1.67,
      "text": "Is that okay?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0008",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 60.14,
      "end_seconds": 67.85,
      "duration_seconds": 7.71,
      "text": "I'll explain what these mean in a moment. How many days or weeks has it been?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0009",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 68.7,
      "end_seconds": 72.42,
      "duration_seconds": 3.72,
      "text": "It's been going on for three weeks."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0010",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 74.23,
      "end_seconds": 78.27,
      "duration_seconds": 4.04,
      "text": "Alright, how strong would you say it is?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0011",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 81.0,
      "end_seconds": 82.08,
      "duration_seconds": 1.08,
      "text": "Mostly mild."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0012",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 82.86,
      "end_seconds": 85.39,
      "duration_seconds": 2.53,
      "text": "How often do you get it?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0013",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 87.42,
      "end_seconds": 89.84,
      "duration_seconds": 2.42,
      "text": "I'd say on and off."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0014",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 90.46,
      "end_seconds": 94.22,
      "duration_seconds": 3.76,
      "text": "Has there been blurred vision in one eye too?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0015",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 95.99,
      "end_seconds": 104.37,
      "duration_seconds": 8.38,
      "text": "Yes, actually. As for blurred vision in one eye, pretty mild, if I'm being honest."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0016",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 106.34,
      "end_seconds": 109.95,
      "duration_seconds": 3.61,
      "text": "Alright, any weight loss, fever or shoulder stiffness?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0017",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 110.89,
      "end_seconds": 116.79,
      "duration_seconds": 5.9,
      "text": "No weight loss, fever or shoulder stiffness, none of it."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0018",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 118.82,
      "end_seconds": 120.51,
      "duration_seconds": 1.69,
      "text": "How's your breathing otherwise?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0019",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 121.86,
      "end_seconds": 123.8,
      "duration_seconds": 1.94,
      "text": "No problems with breathing."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0020",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 124.95,
      "end_seconds": 128.0,
      "duration_seconds": 3.05,
      "text": "And your skin, any changes there?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0021",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 129.03,
      "end_seconds": 129.98,
      "duration_seconds": 0.95,
      "text": "No rashes."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0022",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 138.3,
      "end_seconds": 141.07,
      "duration_seconds": 2.77,
      "text": "Now some background about your lifestyle."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0023",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 142.8,
      "end_seconds": 155.98,
      "duration_seconds": 13.18,
      "text": "I'm a plumber, lots of bending and kneeling. No, I share a house with my brother. I hardly move around during the day."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0024",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 157.7,
      "end_seconds": 159.03,
      "duration_seconds": 1.33,
      "text": "Any previous surgeries?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0025",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 159.62,
      "end_seconds": 162.84,
      "duration_seconds": 3.22,
      "text": "No, I've never been operated on."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0026",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 164.31,
      "end_seconds": 168.45,
      "duration_seconds": 4.14,
      "text": "Are you taking anything regularly, including from the pharmacy?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0027",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 169.84,
      "end_seconds": 173.46,
      "duration_seconds": 3.62,
      "text": "Aspirin, 75 milligrams, once a day."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0028",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 189.4,
      "end_seconds": 191.86,
      "duration_seconds": 2.46,
      "text": "Before we go further, any allergies?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0029",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 193.38,
      "end_seconds": 197.76,
      "duration_seconds": 4.38,
      "text": "Let me think, no, I've never reacted to anything."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0030",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 213.4,
      "end_seconds": 217.02,
      "duration_seconds": 3.62,
      "text": "Any health conditions I should have on record?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0031",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 217.57,
      "end_seconds": 220.97,
      "duration_seconds": 3.4,
      "text": "I have heart disease, for five years."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0032",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 221.73,
      "end_seconds": 228.01,
      "duration_seconds": 6.28,
      "text": "Right, so heart disease is already on your record. We'll keep that in mind today."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0033",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 229.14,
      "end_seconds": 232.13,
      "duration_seconds": 2.99,
      "text": "Okay, time for me to examine you."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0034",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 233.65,
      "end_seconds": 234.82,
      "duration_seconds": 1.17,
      "text": "Breathe out slowly."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0035",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 250.0,
      "end_seconds": 254.29,
      "duration_seconds": 4.29,
      "text": "The temporal artery is hard, tender and has no pulse."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0036",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 257.84,
      "end_seconds": 260.04,
      "duration_seconds": 2.2,
      "text": "You can sit up now."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0037",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 275.75,
      "end_seconds": 282.03,
      "duration_seconds": 6.28,
      "text": "Putting it all together, I'd lean towards possible giant cell arteritis threatening sight."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0038",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 283.83,
      "end_seconds": 285.88,
      "duration_seconds": 2.05,
      "text": "Will it clear up?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0039",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 287.81,
      "end_seconds": 324.26,
      "duration_seconds": 36.45,
      "text": "Nothing I've seen today points to an emergency. It looks like possible giant cell arteritis threatening sight, but I'd like to confirm. I'd like to arrange urgent blood tests for possible giant cell arteritis. I'd like to arrange a temporal artery biopsy for possible giant cell arteritis. I'm prescribing prednisolone, 60 milligrams, once a day, until review. That should help with possible giant cell arteritis. It's a commonly used medicine and most people tolerate it well."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0040",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 325.04,
      "end_seconds": 349.94,
      "duration_seconds": 24.9,
      "text": "Start the steroid today, this is to protect your sight. I'm going to send a referral to the rheumatology team. The thing that would worry me is if you lose vision. If that happens, go to emergency. I'll want another look tomorrow. I think we're done unless you have questions."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0041",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 350.5,
      "end_seconds": 353.84,
      "duration_seconds": 3.34,
      "text": "Hmm, thank you, doctor, goodbye."
    }
  ]
}